What is Type Casting?
Process of converting one data type to another data type.
eg  : int data type to float data type

widening typecasting : 
1.automatically converts small data type to large data type
2.no data loss
3.also called as implicit typecasting 
eg :
int a = 100;
long l = a;

narrowing typecasting :
1. also called as explicit typecasting
2. it is done manually by the programmer
3. loss of data because large data is converted into small data type
eg :
double num = 10.75;
int value = (int) num;
System.out.println(value);  // Output: 10

what is access modifiers ?
*Access modifiers are keywords used to control who can access variables, methods, and classes
*They help in security and restricting unwanted access
*Types: public, private, protected, default
public → can be accessed from anywhere (any class, any package)
private → can be accessed only inside the same class
protected → can be accessed in same package and by child classes
default (no keyword) → can be accessed only within the same package

What is a String ?
A String is a sequence of characters (like text).
It is used to store words, names, or sentences.
In Java, String is an object and immutable.

what is concade ?
Concatenation (concade) means joining two or more strings together
String s = "hello";
s = s.concat(" world");
System.out.println(s);

what is == and equals() ?
== is used to compare memory/reference (address) of objects
equals() is used to compare actual content (values) of objects
For strings: == may give false even if values are same

