What is StringBuffer?
StringBuffer is a class used to create mutable strings (can be changed after creation)
It is thread-safe → safe to use in multi-threaded programs
Methods like append(), insert(), delete() modify the same object

What is StringBuilder?
StringBuilder is also a mutable string class
It is not thread-safe → faster than StringBuffer
Used when performance is important and no multiple threads

Key Difference
StringBuffer → thread-safe, slower
StringBuilder → not thread-safe, faster
Both allow modifying string without creating new objects

When to use
Use StringBuffer → when working with multiple threads (safety needed)
Use StringBuilder → when working with single thread (better performance)

Example
StringBuffer sb1 = new StringBuffer("Hello");
sb1.append(" World");

StringBuilder sb2 = new StringBuilder("Hi");
sb2.append(" Java");

System.out.println(sb1); // Hello World
System.out.println(sb2); // Hi Java
